		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Soapbox derby]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=17192#p17192"><![CDATA[
First you need to change the ratio between the rope and the axle. Note the following systems that reduces the turning ratio (i.e. a large steering wheel turn equals a smaller axle/wheel movement: <a href="http://www.leany.com/images/types_final.jpg" class="postlink">http://www.leany.com/images/types_final.jpg</a><br><br>Next you need axle stops to prevent the axle from excessive turning (i.e. "flipping" your racer).  Note the "bolts with nuts" on either side of the axle: <a href="http://aasbd.com/docs/Stock_Plans.pdf" class="postlink">http://aasbd.com/docs/Stock_Plans.pdf</a>.<br><br>If you want to go fast let me know.<br><br>TXDERBY<br>Crew Chief, Ultimate Speed Challenge - our team hold the current gravity world speed record (there have been over 1 million teams that have attempted to set world gravity speed record)<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6247">TXDERBY</a> — Tue Jan 26, 2010 9:33 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
